THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

The MIT terms above cover the original work in this repository. Some material
is third-party and keeps its own terms. The README section "Third-party
material and attribution" is the authoritative list; the two items that place
conditions on redistribution are repeated here.

1. Toxtree (GPL-2.0), (c) Ideaconsult Ltd. and contributors.
   Three SMARTS patterns in p62_toxicity_alerts.py were transcribed verbatim
   from the Toxtree 3.1.0 source tree (mutant/rules/): the azide/triazene
   alert and the acyl halide alert. Each is marked with a source comment at
   its point of definition. Three further patterns are narrowed variants of
   Toxtree patterns and are likewise marked. The two fused-polycyclic-
   aromatic alerts are an independent RDKit reimplementation of the Toxtree
   decision logic, not a transcription.
   No part of the Toxtree distribution itself is included in or distributed
   with this repository.

2. Ames mutagenicity dataset, compiled by Therapeutics Data Commons
   (doi:10.7910/DVN/21LKWG), no licence stated by the compiler.
   Neither the structures nor the labels are redistributed here. Only
   data/ames_split_manifest.csv is included: InChIKeys, labels and the
   train/validation assignment, sufficient to rebuild the splits from the
   source dataset.

Per-compound predictions from Derek Nexus and Sarah Nexus (Lhasa Limited)
were generated under licence and are NOT included in this repository.
